    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure-based level-4 rule in the one place that owns membership-level derivation, `MembershipLevel.java`:\n\n- **Level 4 now requires tenure > 365 days.** Added a `TENURE_DAYS = 365` constant and a private `hasTenure(registrationDate, asOf)` helper that measures days from the owner's registration date via `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(...)` and returns true only when it exceeds 365 (false when either date is absent).\n- **The creation-time factors (email, no-namesake) cap at 3** (`NEW_OWNER_MAX`), and tenure adds the final step to `MAX = 4`. Since a newly created owner has zero tenure, it can never exceed level 3 \u2014 so a new owner with an email and `namesakeCount == 0` lands at exactly 3, matching the spec.\n- Followed the existing `AgeBand` idiom: a no-arg `of(Owner)` delegating to `LocalDate.now()` plus a testable `of(Owner, LocalDate asOf)` overload, keeping all the logic in this small single-responsibility util rather than spreading it into the mapper.\n- Updated the stale \"1 to 3\" javadoc in `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel` and the class javadoc to reflect the new tenure factor.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` test and the full suite pass (BUILD SUCCESS).",
